  "answer": "Project Zenith is an innovative technology initiative leveraging AI, IoT, and Web3, aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility. The project is led by Marcus Cole, with Omar Jensen as the lead developer. It officially initiated in Q3 2023, following a design phase and moving into development. Key milestones include the approval of a $2M budget by the executive board and a $15,000 training budget for coding teams and project managers. The team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing. Strategic partnerships have been established, notably with TechInnovate, an AI research leader. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% increase in efficiency through proposed AI algorithms, to be discussed in an upcoming meeting on August 5th."
